# Triple review — one Lead, three independent reviewers
#
# The Lead does the work; three Reviewers each look at it independently,
# each on a different provider. Different models have different,
# uncorrelated blind spots -- a bug or bad design that one model waves
# through often gets caught by another. Use this when the cost of a miss is
# high enough to be worth three separate opinions instead of one.
#
# This file uses ${Provider1..3}/${Model1..3} placeholders instead of naming
# a specific provider -- `lmctl quickrun` fills them in with YOUR configured
# providers/models (recorded by `lmctl init`), so this exact file works
# whether you have one provider or several -- with only one provider
# configured, all three reviewers resolve to it, and you're back to a single
# opinion; the value of this pattern grows with how many providers you have.
# See https://lmctl.com/lmctl/docs/manuals/teamfile-format for what a
# _MEMBER_ line means and how to customize this after it's seeded.

_MEMBER_ alias=Lead      provider=${Provider1} model="${Model1}"
_MEMBER_ alias=Reviewer1 provider=${Provider1} model="${Model1}"
_MEMBER_ alias=Reviewer2 provider=${Provider2} model="${Model2}"
_MEMBER_ alias=Reviewer3 provider=${Provider3} model="${Model3}"
